# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Client-exposed values. These MUST be prefixed with VITE_ or Vite will not
# expose them to the bundle. Everything here is public — never put a secret.
#
# That is the whole client surface. Authentication is Supabase Auth, so there is
# no third-party provider, no publishable key from elsewhere, and nothing to
# configure in a second dashboard.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# Optional. Setting both adds a "Continue as demo subscriber" button to the
# sign-in page, which signs in to a pre-filled account in one click — useful for
# a reviewer. OMIT BOTH IN PRODUCTION and the button does not render, so no demo
# credentials are baked into the bundle.
VITE_DEMO_EMAIL=
VITE_DEMO_PASSWORD=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Server-only. Used exclusively by the functions in /api — never imported by
# anything under /src, and never prefixed with VITE_.
#
# The new-format secret key (sb_secret_…) replaces the legacy service_role key.
# It bypasses Row Level Security entirely.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key

# Razorpay, test mode.
#
# THE PLAN IDS ARE OPTIONAL, and they select the billing mode:
#
#   both plan ids set  → auto-renewing Razorpay subscription. Razorpay holds an
#                        e-mandate and charges each cycle itself
#                        (this is the PRD's "handles renewal").
#   otherwise          → one-off orders. Works on any Razorpay account, but
#                        nothing renews and the subscriber pays again when the
#                        period ends.
#
# Order mode is the default because Razorpay gates the Subscriptions product
# behind account activation on some accounts: there, POST /v1/plans and
# /v1/subscriptions return 401 while /v1/orders returns 200. Setting the two plan
# ids later switches modes with no code change.
#
# Create plans (Subscriptions → Plans, or POST /v1/plans) with amounts matching
# api/_lib/pricing.ts: ₹499 monthly, ₹4,999 yearly. The plan is authoritative for
# money; the constants only describe it.
#
# The webhook secret is likewise only needed in subscription mode, since the
# webhook is what activates and renews a subscription.
#
# The key id reaches the browser through the /api/billing response, so it does
# not need a VITE_ variable.
RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=rzp_test_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
RAZORPAY_PLAN_MONTHLY=
RAZORPAY_PLAN_YEARLY=

CRON_SECRET=generate-a-long-random-string

# Public origin of the deployed site.
SITE_URL=http://localhost:5173
